1
00:00:10,421 --> 00:00:14,647
Most of what a service desk answers
is somebody asking what is happening.

2
00:00:15,102 --> 00:00:21,093
A workspace can carry a portal: a
way in for the people you work for.

3
00:00:21,545 --> 00:00:27,993
You decide who gets in, one client at a
time, and what they are allowed to do once

4
00:00:27,993 --> 00:00:28,465
there.

5
00:00:28,918 --> 00:00:36,474
What they see is theirs and only theirs.
There is no version of this where they see

6
00:00:36,474 --> 00:00:38,113
a neighbour's job.

7
00:00:38,573 --> 00:00:44,239
And they can raise a request, which
arrives as work rather than as a voicemail.

8
00:00:44,693 --> 00:00:48,548
Next: talking to them
inside the job itself.

